### Dynamic process formalization

At any time, groups are intervals of original index order. For group G with rightmost r, position P_G(t)=p_r+v_r t, as long as r is rightmost. If two adjacent groups A,B with reps a,b have left speed <= right, their gap nondecreasing. They are separate now, so gap>d, never merge. If left speed>right, first contact at T(a,b)=max(0,(p_b-p_a-d)/(v_a-v_b)). Since both reps alive and positions linear. Merges happen at earliest such event among adjacent pairs, with simultaneous closure. Our event queue plus batching exactly implements.

